INSERT INTO `faqs` VALUES (65,32,'Can I apply for a mortgage directly or should I use a broker?','At Equifirst Capital Financing we help you compare products, get better deals, and manage paperwork — at no cost to you.','2025-08-05 12:05:02','2025-08-05 12:05:02'),(66,32,'Can I use a mortgage to buy a property outside the UAE?','Some banks offer international property financing, but it’s limited and case-specific.','2025-08-05 12:05:36','2025-08-05 12:05:36'),(67,32,'How long does it take to get a mortgage?','Pre-approval takes 2–10 working days; the full process can take 2–4 weeks depending on the case.','2025-08-05 12:06:01','2025-08-05 12:06:01'),(68,32,'Is Sharia-compliant (Islamic) home financing available?','Yes, Islamic banks offer products like Ijara and Murabaha.','2025-08-05 12:06:30','2025-08-05 12:06:30'),(69,32,'Can I assign my own life insurance to the mortgage?','Banks do not allow for the assignment of existing life insurances. However, based on bank approvals, some banks might allow it.','2025-08-05 12:07:02','2025-08-05 12:07:02'),(70,32,'What is Property insurance?','Property insurance protects the bank and the borrower in case of the property no longer being habitable. In the unfortunate event that the property is no longer habitable, the property insurance is invoked, and the outstanding loan is settled – making the property free of mortgage and lien. It is calculated based on the property value.','2025-08-05 12:08:39','2025-08-05 12:08:39'),(71,32,'What is life insurance?','Life insurance protects the bank and the borrower in case of death. In the unfortunate event of the borrower’s death, the life insurance is invoked, and the outstanding loan is settled – making the property free of mortgage and lien.  It is calculated based on the outstanding loan amount.','2025-08-05 12:09:10','2025-08-05 12:09:10'),(72,32,'How are mortgage repayments calculated?','They depend on the loan amount, interest rate, and loan tenure. The Equifirst calculator can be used to estimate the monthly installments.','2025-08-05 12:24:15','2025-08-05 12:24:15'),(73,32,'How much can I borrow for a mortgage?','It depends on your income, liabilities, and the property’s value—up to 80% of the value in most cases.','2025-08-05 12:24:51','2025-08-05 12:24:51'),(74,32,'Can I get a mortgage for off-plan properties?','Yes, some banks offer financing for under-construction properties from approved developers.','2025-08-05 12:25:21','2025-08-05 12:25:21'),(75,32,'How long is mortgage pre-approval valid for?','Typically between 60–90 days depending on the bank.','2025-08-05 12:25:45','2025-08-05 12:25:45'),(76,32,'What is the difference between an Approval in Principle (AIP) and a Preapproval?','Approval in Principle is usually not underwritten by credit and the bank has the right to decline the approval at a later stage.   A Preapproval is underwritten by credit and as long as the terms of the preapproval are adhered to, the bank will process the loan.','2025-08-05 12:26:14','2025-08-05 12:26:14'),(77,32,'What is mortgage pre-approval?','A bank gives you a conditional approval for a loan amount before you find a property.','2025-08-05 12:26:36','2025-08-05 12:26:36'),(78,32,'What happens if I miss a mortgage payment?','Banks may charge late fees and, if missed repeatedly, your property could be repossessed.','2025-08-05 12:27:00','2025-08-05 12:27:00'),(79,32,'Can I pay off my mortgage early?','Yes, most banks allow for a certain percentage to be made as overpayments each year. However, if you want to settle more than that, banks charge an early settlement fee (typically 1% of the remaining amount or AED 10,000).','2025-08-05 12:27:30','2025-08-05 12:27:30'),(80,32,'What are the types of mortgages available in the UAE?','Fixed-rate, variable-rate, conventional, Islamic Finance, Non Resident, Equity Release, Secondary Market Finance, Handover Finance, Offplan Financing.','2025-08-05 12:28:05','2025-08-05 12:28:05'),(81,32,'Is it better to rent or buy in the UAE?','It depends on your financial goals. Buying helps you build equity, while renting offers flexibility.','2025-08-05 12:28:34','2025-08-05 12:28:34'),(82,32,'Can I get a mortgage as a first-time buyer?','Yes, first-time buyers are eligible as long as they meet income and credit criteria.','2025-08-05 12:29:02','2025-08-05 12:29:02'),(83,32,'How much down payment is needed for a property in the UAE?','For UAE residents, you can need a down payment of 20% for properties valued below AED 5million, and 30% down payment for properties valued higher than AED 5 million.\r\nFor Non residents, typically the down payment is between 35-40%.','2025-08-05 12:29:34','2025-08-05 12:29:34'),(84,32,'What is EIBOR and how does it affect my mortgage?','EIBOR (Emirates Interbank Offered Rate) is the interest rate banks charge each other and is a base for most variable-rate mortgages.','2025-08-05 12:30:03','2025-08-05 12:30:03'),(85,32,'What’s the difference between fixed and variable mortgage rates?','Fixed rates stay the same for a set period; variable rates change based on market conditions like EIBOR.','2025-08-05 12:30:30','2025-08-05 12:30:30'),(86,32,'How long can a self-employed person get a mortgage?','A self employed person can borrow money up to the age of 70, or 25 years which ever comes first.','2025-08-05 12:30:54','2025-08-05 12:33:14'),(87,32,'How long can a salaried person get a mortgage?','A salaried individual can borrow money up to the age of 65, or 25 years which ever comes first. Some banks will allow borrowing up to the age of 70, under special conditions. However, you cannot borrow for more than 25 years.','2025-08-05 12:31:28','2025-08-05 12:31:28'),(88,32,'How does a mortgage work in the UAE?','You borrow money from a bank and repay it monthly with interest over an agreed term, up to 25 years.','2025-08-05 12:33:45','2025-08-05 12:33:45'),(89,32,'What is a mortgage?','A mortgage is a long-term loan used to buy property, where the property itself serves as security for the loan.','2025-08-05 12:34:10','2025-08-05 12:34:10'),(91,31,'Can I get a mortgage if I’m working on commission only?','Unfortunately no.  You require a salary certificate with a minimum salary of AED 10k/month.','2025-08-05 12:46:35','2025-08-05 12:46:35'),(92,31,'Can I apply if I’m retired?','It’s challenging. Most banks require a steady income source, not just savings.','2025-08-05 12:47:13','2025-08-05 12:47:13'),(93,31,'Is there a nationality restriction for mortgage eligibility?','No formal restrictions, but some banks have internal preferences. Most nationalities are accepted.','2025-08-05 12:47:47','2025-08-05 12:47:47'),(94,31,'Can I get a mortgage if I don’t have a UAE bank account?','If you are a UAE resident, you need to have a UAE bank account in which your salary or business income is being credited, in order to get a mortgage.','2025-08-05 12:48:32','2025-08-05 12:48:32'),(95,31,'Can a company sponsor my mortgage?','Unfortunately, your company cannot sponsor your mortgage.','2025-08-05 12:49:11','2025-08-05 12:49:11'),(96,31,'What if I have bounced cheques or missed payments?','These show up in your credit report and may negatively affect your application.','2025-08-05 12:49:38','2025-08-05 12:49:38'),(97,31,'Can I apply if I already have a mortgage?','Yes, but your DBR and property portfolio will be assessed.','2025-08-05 12:50:11','2025-08-05 12:50:11'),(98,31,'What is DBR and how is it calculated?','DBR = your total monthly liabilities ÷ monthly income. It must stay below 50%.','2025-08-05 12:51:01','2025-08-07 10:31:00'),(99,31,'Will having a loan or credit card impact my application?','Yes. Existing liabilities reduce your borrowing capacity based on your Debt Burden Ratio (DBR). As a central bank rule, you cannot borrow more than 50% of your monthly income.','2025-08-05 12:51:39','2025-08-05 12:51:39'),(100,31,'What is the minimum credit score required?','Typically 550+, but banks prefer 650+ for better terms. Use Al Etihad Credit Bureau to check.','2025-08-05 12:52:06','2025-08-05 12:52:06'),(101,31,'Does my credit score affect my eligibility?','Yes. A low score can reduce your chances or lead to higher interest rates.','2025-08-05 12:52:43','2025-08-05 12:52:43'),(102,31,'Can I apply with a co-applicant?','Yes. Co-applicants help boost income eligibility and are often spouses or close family.','2025-08-05 12:53:13','2025-08-05 12:53:13'),(103,31,'Can freelancers or consultants apply?','Currently, freelancers are not eligible for a mortgage.','2025-08-05 12:53:38','2025-08-05 12:53:38'),(104,31,'Can I get a mortgage if I’m self-employed?','Yes. You’ll need trade license, audit reports, and bank statements to show consistent income.','2025-08-05 12:54:04','2025-08-05 12:54:04'),(105,31,'Do I need to be employed in the UAE?','For UAE resident mortgages, yes. For non-resident mortgages, income from your home country is considered.','2025-08-05 12:54:36','2025-08-05 12:54:36'),(106,31,'Is there an age limit for getting a mortgage?','Yes. Most banks require repayment by age 65 for salaried, and 70 for self-employed applicants.  However, there are some banks that can extend the age for salaried individuals to 70yrs, but not more than 25 years total.','2025-08-05 12:55:04','2025-08-05 12:55:04'),(107,31,'Can I apply if I just joined a new job?','Yes you can. Most banks require 3-6months of employment. However, there are banks that will provide a mortgage to clients with 1 months of employment in a new company.','2025-08-05 12:55:49','2025-08-05 12:55:49'),(108,31,'What is the minimum income required to apply?','Salaried: typically AED 15K/month, but some banks are willing to provide mortgages to clients with a salary of AED 10K/month; Self-employed: AED 40K/month — varies by bank.','2025-08-05 12:56:25','2025-08-05 12:56:25'),(109,31,'Can non-residents apply for a mortgage in the UAE?','Yes, but banks typically require a larger down payment (35–40%) and stricter documentation.','2025-08-05 12:56:53','2025-08-05 12:56:53'),(110,31,'Am I eligible for a mortgage in the UAE?','If you\'re over 21, have a stable income, and meet bank criteria, you’re likely eligible.','2025-08-05 12:57:17','2025-08-05 12:57:17'),(111,14,'Can a resident apply for a mortgage on behalf of a non-resident family member?','No — the applicant must be the one taking the loan. You can assist, but cannot apply as a proxy.','2025-08-05 14:55:09','2025-08-05 14:55:09'),(112,14,'What if I have an existing mortgage in my home country?','Your credit eligibility is based on your UAE liabilities and income.','2025-08-05 14:56:12','2025-08-05 14:56:12'),(113,14,'Can I get a mortgage on a freehold property if I’m not a GCC national?','Yes, expats can buy freehold properties in designated zones with full financing options.','2025-08-05 14:57:35','2025-08-05 14:57:35'),(114,14,'What if I’m self-employed and my income is irregular?','For self-employed clients, the bank considers 1-2 years of revenue generation.   I need not be consistent monthly.','2025-08-05 14:58:09','2025-08-05 14:58:09'),(115,14,'Can a non-resident apply without visiting the UAE?','Yes — some banks allow Power of Attorney (POA) or remote onboarding with notarized documents. It depends on the bank.','2025-08-05 14:58:41','2025-08-05 14:58:41'),(116,14,'I am on a sabbatical — can I still apply?','Not unless you can show consistent, passive income or savings. Active income is typically required.','2025-08-05 14:59:07','2025-08-05 14:59:07'),(117,14,'Can I use cryptocurrency as part of my down payment?','No. UAE banks only accept traceable, legal sources of income in AED or foreign fiat currencies.','2025-08-05 14:59:40','2025-08-05 14:59:40'),(118,14,'Are mortgages available for properties outside the UAE?','UAE banks only finance UAE-based properties. For overseas properties, financing must be done through local institutions abroad.','2025-08-05 15:00:09','2025-08-05 15:00:09'),(119,14,'What if I want to buy with a sibling or parent?','Yes this is possible.','2025-08-05 15:00:38','2025-08-05 15:00:38'),(120,14,'Can I get a mortgage while on a freelance visa?','Currently freelance visas are not eligible for mortgage.','2025-08-05 15:01:04','2025-08-05 15:01:04'),(121,14,'Can I use my company as the mortgage applicant?','Yes you can.   However, in this case the company will be reviewed by credit for eligibility.','2025-08-05 15:01:46','2025-08-05 15:01:46'),(122,14,'Can I get a mortgage without a UAE credit history?','Non-residents can apply without UAE credit history, but residents will need at least 3–6 months of credit footprint in the UAE.','2025-08-05 15:02:13','2025-08-05 15:02:13'),(123,14,'What if I have multiple nationalities?','You should apply using your UAE resident status. If you’re a non-resident, choose the nationality most favorable for documentation.','2025-08-05 15:02:39','2025-08-05 15:02:39'),(124,14,'Can I get a mortgage if I’ve just changed jobs?','Yes, but most banks prefer 3-6 months of employment history. Some will consider probation cases with additional documentation.','2025-08-05 15:03:07','2025-08-05 15:03:07'),(125,14,'Can I buy property under my child\'s name?','Not with a mortgage — banks require the applicant to be a legal adult with income. You can purchase outright under a child’s name.','2025-08-05 15:03:37','2025-08-05 15:03:37'),(126,14,'What if one spouse is not earning — can we still apply jointly?','Yes, but only the income-earning spouse’s profile will be assessed. The second applicant may be listed for ownership purposes.','2025-08-05 15:04:04','2025-08-05 15:04:04'),(127,14,'Can two friends apply jointly for a mortgage?','No. Banks only allow joint applications for married couples and immediate family members.','2025-08-05 15:06:43','2025-08-05 15:06:43'),(128,15,'Do banks blacklist certain employers or countries?','Some banks have approved employer lists or restricted countries for compliance. A broker can help filter accordingly.','2025-08-05 15:07:35','2025-08-05 15:07:35'),(129,15,'Which banks are best for non-residents?','HSBC, Mashreq, ENBD and a few others offer mortgage products for non-residents with stricter requirements and lower LTV.','2025-08-05 15:08:14','2025-08-05 15:08:14'),(130,15,'Can I use a property under construction for mortgage?','Only if the project is approved by the bank — off-plan financing rules differ by lender and developer.','2025-08-05 15:08:38','2025-08-05 15:08:38'),(131,15,'Are there banks that allow salary transfer as a requirement?','Some banks (especially for better rates) require salary transfer, while others accept non-transfer clients at slightly higher rates.','2025-08-05 15:35:11','2025-08-05 15:35:11'),(132,15,'Do any banks allow you to refinance without early settlement fees?','Some banks waive it during internal refinancing or buyout promotions.','2025-08-05 15:36:41','2025-08-05 15:36:41'),(133,15,'Which banks charge early settlement fees?','Most banks charge 1%, capped at AED 10,000 — but some waive or reduce it depending on the case.','2025-08-05 15:37:34','2025-08-05 15:37:34'),(134,15,'Are fixed rates the same across all banks?','No — fixed periods and rates vary. Some offer 2-year fixed, others offer 3–5 years, with different pricing.','2025-08-05 15:38:14','2025-08-05 15:38:14'),(135,15,'Do all banks require property valuation?','Yes — and most banks appoint their own valuer. Fees and timelines vary.','2025-08-05 15:38:49','2025-08-05 15:38:49'),(136,15,'Do any banks give better rates for high-income clients?','Yes — private banking divisions or premier accounts may access preferential rates.','2025-08-05 15:39:17','2025-08-05 15:39:17'),(137,15,'Are there banks that offer 30-year mortgage tenures?','The maximum tenor is 300 months.','2025-08-05 15:39:48','2025-08-05 15:39:48'),(138,15,'Which banks accept joint applications with a non-spouse?','A joint mortgage can only be done with immediate and direct family members, such as, parents, siblings, children (above age 21).','2025-08-05 15:40:19','2025-08-05 15:40:19'),(139,15,'Do all banks require audit reports for self-employed applicants?','Not all — some may accept VAT returns or bank statements, but audited reports improve chances and limits.','2025-08-05 15:40:58','2025-08-05 15:40:58'),(140,15,'Which banks accept self-employed applicants easily?','Banks like RAKBANK and Mashreq are more flexible with self-employed profiles, especially with audited financials.','2025-08-05 15:41:30','2025-08-05 15:41:30'),(141,15,'Do some banks have lower salary thresholds for eligibility?','Yes. Some banks require AED 10K, others AED 15K or more, depending on profile and employer.','2025-08-05 15:41:59','2025-08-05 15:41:59'),(142,15,'Can I apply to multiple banks at once?','Yes — especially through a broker. This increases your chances and allows rate comparisons, without damaging your credit.','2025-08-05 15:42:30','2025-08-05 15:42:30'),(143,15,'Do Islamic banks require a different set of documents?','The core requirements are similar, but contracts and terminology differ (e.g., Ijara, Murabaha instead of \"loan\").','2025-08-05 15:42:55','2025-08-05 15:42:55'),(144,15,'Which banks offer Islamic mortgages?','Banks like ADIB, DIB, and Emirates Islamic offer Sharia-compliant financing with different structures from conventional loans.','2025-08-05 15:43:21','2025-08-05 15:43:21'),(145,15,'Are there banks that allow 85% financing for expats?','85% financing is only allowed for UAE nationals on their first property.  Standard expat financing is capped at 80% for properties under AED 5M.','2025-08-05 15:43:45','2025-08-05 15:43:45'),(146,15,'Which bank gives the fastest mortgage approvals?','It varies. Some banks like Emirates NBD or Mashreq have faster processes for salaried clients. At Equifirst Capital Financing, we guide you through the whole process and help select the right bank based on your profile.','2025-08-05 15:44:12','2025-08-05 15:44:12'),(147,15,'Do all banks in the UAE have the same mortgage policies?','No — each bank sets its own criteria for eligibility, documentation, rate structures, and approval timelines.','2025-08-05 15:44:37','2025-08-05 15:44:37'),(148,16,'“The broker’s fee is too high — I’d rather do it myself.”','At Equifirst Capital Financing, we do not charge a fee for traditional mortgage services.   In addition, often we save you far more in rate negotiations, process speed, and avoid costly errors.','2025-08-05 15:45:13','2025-08-05 15:45:13'),(149,16,'“I can’t get a mortgage if I have bounced cheques or late payments.”','Not always true. Some banks may still approve you depending on recency, reason, and overall profile.','2025-08-05 15:45:39','2025-08-05 15:45:39'),(150,16,'“Islamic and conventional mortgages are the same.”','They’re structured differently. Islamic mortgages follow Sharia law and use profit-based models.','2025-08-05 15:46:04','2025-08-05 15:46:04'),(151,16,'“Down payment must be paid to the bank.”','No. Down payment is paid directly to the seller. Banks finance the remaining loan amount.','2025-08-05 15:46:34','2025-08-05 15:46:34'),(152,16,'“I’ll wait until I find a property to apply.”','Bad idea. Pre-approval helps you move faster and negotiate better when you find a property.','2025-08-05 16:02:48','2025-08-05 16:02:48'),(153,16,'“Mortgage approvals take too long in the UAE.”','With complete documents and broker support, approvals can take as little as 5–7 working days.','2025-08-05 16:03:21','2025-08-05 16:03:21'),(154,16,'“If my friend refers me to their banker, I’ll get better service.”','Possibly — but a broker gives you access to all banks, not just one relationship manager.','2025-08-05 16:03:50','2025-08-05 16:03:50'),(155,16,'“I’m a UAE resident, so I automatically qualify.”','Residency helps, but you still need to meet income, credit, and documentation criteria.','2025-08-05 16:04:12','2025-08-05 16:04:12'),(156,16,'“A higher salary always means a bigger loan.”','Loan size also depends on other liabilities, tenure, and bank caps (like max 50% of income).','2025-08-05 16:04:39','2025-08-05 16:04:39'),(157,16,'“Refinancing is too expensive and not worth it.”','Depends on your case. The long-term savings from a lower rate can far outweigh short-term fees.','2025-08-05 16:05:03','2025-08-05 16:05:03'),(158,16,'“If I apply to multiple banks, I’ll get blacklisted.”','Applying through a broker manages this risk. Multiple blind applications can hurt your score.','2025-08-05 16:05:25','2025-08-05 16:05:25'),(159,16,'“Banks won’t approve me if I have a car loan.”','Not true. As long as your debt-to-income ratio is within limits, you can still qualify.','2025-08-05 16:05:56','2025-08-05 16:05:56'),(160,16,'“If I don’t have a credit card, my credit score is perfect.”','Not always. No credit history = no score. Some credit activity is needed to establish a positive score.','2025-08-05 16:06:25','2025-08-05 16:06:25'),(161,16,'“Self-employed clients can’t get mortgages.”','False. Self-employed clients can qualify with proper financials, VAT, audit reports, and consistent income.','2025-08-05 16:06:52','2025-08-05 16:06:52'),(162,16,'“A higher down payment will reduce my interest rate.”','Not necessarily. It may improve eligibility, but rate depends on the bank\'s pricing and your profile.','2025-08-05 16:07:15','2025-08-05 16:07:15'),(163,16,'“My friend got a 1.99% rate — I should get the same.”','Rates depend on profile, income, property type, bank policy, and market timing','2025-08-05 16:07:40','2025-08-05 16:07:40'),(164,16,'“Fixed rates mean my rate will never change.”','Fixed rates are for a defined period (e.g., 2–5 years). After that, it often switches to a variable rate.','2025-08-05 16:08:02','2025-08-05 16:08:02'),(165,16,'“Pre-approval means I’m guaranteed a loan.”','No. It’s conditional and subject to final document checks, valuation, and underwriting.','2025-08-05 16:08:29','2025-08-05 16:08:29'),(166,16,'“I have a good salary, so I’ll get approved easily.”','Income is just one factor. Banks also consider credit history, liabilities, employment type, and residency.','2025-08-05 16:08:53','2025-08-05 16:08:53'),(167,16,'“I don’t need a mortgage broker — I’ll just go to my bank.”','Your bank offers only their own products. A broker compares all banks and helps negotiate better terms.','2025-08-05 16:09:17','2025-08-05 16:09:17'),(168,18,'What if the new bank rejects my refinance application?','You’ll continue with your current lender, but a broker can help you explore other banks with different criteria.','2025-08-05 16:12:32','2025-08-05 16:12:32'),(169,18,'Can refinancing extend my loan tenure?','Yes. You can renegotiate the duration to reduce monthly payments—up to age limits allowed by banks.','2025-08-05 16:13:31','2025-08-05 16:13:31'),(170,18,'Are there brokers who specialize in refinancing?','Yes. Mortgage brokers can help compare offers and manage the full switch on your behalf.','2025-08-05 16:14:25','2025-08-05 16:14:25'),(171,18,'Will I need a new mortgage registration with the DLD?','Yes. Refinancing with a new bank requires cancellation and re-registration, along with applicable fees.','2025-08-05 16:15:02','2025-08-05 16:15:02'),(172,18,'What is the difference between refinancing and restructuring?','Refinancing replaces your loan. Restructuring modifies the current loan terms due to financial hardship.','2025-08-05 16:16:05','2025-08-05 16:16:05'),(173,18,'Can I refinance if my property is under construction?','Usually no. Most banks only allow refinancing on completed, handed-over properties.','2025-08-05 16:16:48','2025-08-05 16:16:48'),(174,18,'Is there a minimum time I must wait before refinancing?','Some banks require you to wait 6–12 months from your original mortgage date.','2025-08-05 16:17:20','2025-08-05 16:17:20'),(175,18,'Can I refinance to switch from Islamic to conventional banking (or vice versa)?','Yes, as long as the bank you’re moving to supports the switch and your profile qualifies.','2025-08-05 16:17:48','2025-08-05 16:17:48'),(176,18,'Can I refinance if I’ve missed mortgage payments?','It’s harder. Banks prefer clients with clean payment histories, but brokers can help position your case.','2025-08-05 16:18:15','2025-08-05 16:18:15'),(177,18,'How long does the refinance process take?','Around 2–4 weeks depending on bank processing times, documentation, and property valuation.','2025-08-05 16:19:20','2025-08-05 16:19:20'),(178,18,'Will my credit score be affected if I refinance?','A small, temporary drop may occur due to the inquiry—but it\'s generally not significant if managed well.','2025-08-05 16:19:57','2025-08-05 16:19:57'),(179,18,'Can I refinance to increase my loan amount?','Yes, if you qualify based on income and the new property valuation.','2025-08-05 16:20:29','2025-08-05 16:20:29'),(180,18,'What is equity release during refinancing?','If your property has appreciated in value, you can borrow against that increased equity for other purposes.','2025-08-05 16:25:41','2025-08-05 16:25:41'),(181,18,'Are there fees involved in refinancing?','Yes. Common fees include valuation, processing, early settlement, mortgage registration, and possibly broker fees.','2025-08-05 16:26:15','2025-08-05 16:26:15'),(182,18,'Will I need to reapply and submit documents?','Yes. A refinance is treated as a new application with full documentation and credit checks.','2025-08-05 16:26:38','2025-08-05 16:26:38'),(183,18,'Do I need a property valuation for refinancing?','Yes. The new bank will usually do a fresh valuation to determine the loan amount they can offer.','2025-08-05 16:27:06','2025-08-05 16:27:06'),(184,18,'Can I refinance during my fixed-rate period?','Yes, but banks often charge early settlement penalties—usually around 1% of the loan balance.','2025-08-05 16:27:31','2025-08-05 16:27:31'),(185,18,'Why would I refinance my mortgage?','To lower your interest rate, reduce your monthly payments, switch from variable to fixed, or release equity.','2025-08-05 16:27:58','2025-08-05 16:27:58'),(186,18,'What is a mortgage buyout?','A buyout is when a different bank pays off your existing loan and gives you a new mortgage, often with better terms.','2025-08-05 16:28:22','2025-08-05 16:28:22'),(187,18,'What is mortgage refinancing?','Refinancing means replacing your current home loan with a new one—either with the same bank or a different one.','2025-08-05 16:28:51','2025-08-05 16:28:51'),(188,19,'Do I need life or property insurance for all mortgage products?','Yes. Banks usually require both, and many bundle the insurance into the mortgage application process.','2025-08-05 16:29:32','2025-08-05 16:29:32'),(189,19,'What is a top-up mortgage?','A top-up lets you borrow additional funds against an existing property — subject to revaluation and eligibility.','2025-08-05 16:30:05','2025-08-05 16:30:05'),(190,19,'What happens when the fixed period ends?','Your mortgage typically switches to a variable rate unless you refinance or renegotiate with your bank.','2025-08-05 16:30:34','2025-08-05 16:30:34'),(191,19,'How long can I fix my mortgage rate for?','Fixed-rate periods range from 1 to 5 years. After that, the rate usually reverts to variable unless renegotiated.','2025-08-05 16:31:05','2025-08-05 16:31:05'),(192,19,'Do any banks offer cashback or rewards with mortgages?','Yes. Some offer cashback on disbursal, air miles, or fee waivers as part of promotions.','2025-08-05 16:31:30','2025-08-05 16:31:30'),(193,19,'Can I get a construction mortgage to build on my own plot?','A few banks offer this. Usually split into land finance + construction stages, requiring architectural plans and permits.','2025-08-05 16:31:56','2025-08-05 16:31:56'),(194,19,'Are there bank tie-ups with specific developers?','Yes. Banks often have partnerships with developers like Emaar, Sobha, or Damac — offering faster approvals or better terms.','2025-08-05 16:32:19','2025-08-05 16:32:19'),(195,19,'Are there special mortgage products for UAE nationals?','Some banks offer exclusive rates and terms for Emiratis, including longer tenures and lower down payment options.','2025-08-05 16:32:46','2025-08-05 16:32:46'),(196,19,'Can I get a mortgage jointly with a spouse or family member?','Yes, joint applications are allowed — subject to eligibility and relationship proof (marriage cert, etc.).','2025-08-05 16:33:23','2025-08-05 16:33:23'),(197,19,'Do banks offer salary-transfer and non-salary-transfer options?','Yes. Salary-transfer options often have better rates, but many banks also provide non-transfer products (usually at higher rates).','2025-08-05 16:33:59','2025-08-05 16:33:59'),(198,19,'Are there green or sustainable mortgage options in the UAE?','A few banks offer discounts on eco-friendly homes — often tied to DEWA efficiency ratings or LEED certifications.','2025-08-05 16:34:34','2025-08-05 16:34:34'),(199,19,'What is a rent-to-own mortgage?','Not a bank product — it’s a developer model where part of your rent is credited toward eventual ownership.','2025-08-05 16:34:58','2025-08-05 16:34:58'),(200,19,'What is an interest-only mortgage?','You pay only interest for a set period (e.g., 2–5 years), then start repaying the principal. Rare in UAE and usually for investors.','2025-08-05 16:35:21','2025-08-05 16:35:21'),(201,19,'Are there special mortgage products for first-time buyers?','Some banks offer lower rates, reduced fees, or relaxed eligibility criteria for first-time buyers.','2025-08-05 16:35:49','2025-08-05 16:35:49'),(202,19,'Can I get a mortgage for an off-plan property?','Yes, some banks finance under-construction properties, often with staged disbursements tied to developer progress.','2025-08-05 16:36:13','2025-08-05 16:36:13'),(203,19,'How is an Islamic mortgage different from a conventional one?','Islamic mortgages follow Shariah principles — no interest is charged. Instead, banks use structures like Ijara or Murabaha (rent or cost-plus).','2025-08-05 16:36:36','2025-08-05 16:36:36'),(204,19,'What is a hybrid mortgage?','A mix of fixed and variable — e.g., fixed for 2 years, then variable. Offers initial stability with future flexibility.','2025-08-05 16:36:56','2025-08-05 16:36:56'),(205,19,'What is a variable-rate mortgage?','The interest rate can change over time, usually linked to EIBOR. Your monthly payments may go up or down.','2025-08-05 16:37:19','2025-08-05 16:37:19'),(206,19,'What is a fixed-rate mortgage?','It means your interest rate remains the same for a set period, usually 1–5 years, making your monthly payments predictable.','2025-08-05 16:37:40','2025-08-05 16:37:40'),(207,19,'What are the main types of mortgages in the UAE?','UAE banks typically offer fixed-rate, variable-rate, hybrid (fixed + variable), and Islamic home financing.','2025-08-05 16:38:06','2025-08-05 16:38:06'),(208,20,'Do banks finance multiple properties at once?','Yes, depending on your eligibility and income. Each property requires separate approval.','2025-08-05 16:38:31','2025-08-05 16:38:31'),(209,20,'What if the property has existing tenants?','Having a tenant does not affect the valuation of a property.','2025-08-05 16:38:59','2025-08-05 16:38:59'),(210,20,'Do banks finance hotel apartments or serviced units?','Some do, but many banks exclude them due to ownership structure and rental models.','2025-08-05 16:39:23','2025-08-05 16:39:23'),(211,20,'Are bank valuations negotiable?','Valuations can be disputed, however, the decision to change the valuation amount is solely on the valuation company.','2025-08-05 16:39:46','2025-08-05 16:39:46'),(212,20,'What is the minimum property value banks will finance?','Generally, banks prefer properties valued at AED 500,000 or higher.','2025-08-05 16:40:10','2025-08-05 16:40:10'),(213,20,'Can I get a mortgage for a commercial property?','Yes, but options are fewer, rates are higher, and down payment requirements are stricter.','2025-08-05 16:40:34','2025-08-05 16:40:34'),(214,20,'Do banks finance properties under construction?','Only if the project is approved by the bank and the developer is on the bank’s panel.','2025-08-05 16:40:56','2025-08-05 16:40:56'),(215,20,'Do I need a valuation for off-plan property?','Not always. Banks may rely on the developer’s pricing, but some still require it.','2025-08-05 16:41:19','2025-08-05 16:41:19'),(216,20,'Is valuation refundable if my mortgage is not approved?','No — valuation fees are non-refundable regardless of the outcome.','2025-08-05 16:41:48','2025-08-05 16:41:48'),(217,20,'How much does a valuation cost?','Typically between AED 2,500 and AED 3,500, depending on the bank and property type.','2025-08-05 16:42:15','2025-08-05 16:42:15'),(218,20,'Can I get a copy of the valuation report?','Yes — the bank or valuer can provide this on request, though not all banks do so by default.','2025-08-05 16:42:36','2025-08-05 16:42:36'),(219,20,'What if the valuation is lower than the purchase price?','You’ll need to pay the difference in cash. Banks finance based on the lower of the two values.','2025-08-05 16:42:59','2025-08-05 16:42:59'),(220,20,'How is property value determined?','Based on location, size, condition, market trends, and recent sales of similar properties.','2025-08-05 16:43:39','2025-08-05 16:43:39'),(221,20,'Who performs the valuation?','Independent valuers appointed by the bank. You usually pay the valuation fee.','2025-08-05 16:44:07','2025-08-05 16:44:07'),(222,20,'What is a property valuation?','A professional assessment of a property’s market value, conducted by the bank to determine how much they’re willing to lend.','2025-08-05 16:44:31','2025-08-05 16:44:31'),(223,20,'Do banks finance leasehold properties?','Some do, depending on the remaining lease term and developer reputation.','2025-08-05 16:44:55','2025-08-05 16:44:55'),(224,20,'What is the difference between freehold and leasehold property?','Freehold means full ownership. Leasehold means you lease the property for a fixed term (e.g., 99 years).','2025-08-05 16:45:18','2025-08-05 16:45:18'),(225,20,'Can I get a mortgage for an off-plan property?','Yes, but fewer banks offer this. Down payment requirements are usually higher, and approval is stricter.','2025-08-05 16:45:41','2025-08-05 16:45:41'),(226,20,'What types of properties can I get a mortgage for in the UAE?','Residential (apartments, villas, townhouses), commercial, off-plan, and completed freehold properties.','2025-08-05 16:46:06','2025-08-05 16:46:06'),(227,30,'Can I apply jointly with my spouse if only one of us works?','Yes. The working spouse is the main applicant, while the other can be a co-borrower for ownership purposes.','2025-08-07 10:31:58','2025-08-07 10:31:58'),(228,30,'Does it matter if my income is paid in a foreign currency?','Some banks accept foreign income but may apply conversion and risk buffers.','2025-08-07 10:32:35','2025-08-07 10:32:35'),(229,30,'Can I apply using overseas income?','Yes, for non-resident mortgages — but banks require notarized documents and translated bank statements.','2025-08-07 10:33:07','2025-08-07 10:33:07'),(230,30,'Can I apply if I’m on a sabbatical or currently unemployed?','Generally no, unless you have strong alternative income such as rental, or a co-applicant with income.','2025-08-07 10:33:41','2025-08-07 10:33:41'),(231,30,'What if I’m a partner in a business?','Banks may assess your ownership percentage, dividends, and business health before approving.','2025-08-07 10:34:09','2025-08-07 10:34:09'),(232,30,'Do I need to be VAT registered if self-employed?','Not always, but being VAT-registered adds credibility and helps banks validate revenue.','2025-08-07 10:34:42','2025-08-07 10:34:42'),(233,30,'What documents are needed for rental income?','Tenancy contracts, Ejari, title deeds, and 6 months of bank statements showing rental deposits.','2025-08-07 10:35:13','2025-08-07 10:35:13'),(234,30,'Can I get a mortgage if I own rental properties?','Yes. Rental income is considered as self-employed income if documented properly.','2025-08-07 10:35:39','2025-08-07 10:35:39'),(235,30,'Can I apply if I have multiple jobs or income sources?','Yes. As long as all income is declared and supported with documentation. Additional income such as commissions, bonuses and rental income can be considered.','2025-08-07 10:36:12','2025-08-07 10:36:12'),(236,30,'What if I earn variable income (commission, bonuses)?','Unfortunately no. You require a salary certificate with a minimum salary of AED 10k/month.','2025-08-07 10:36:47','2025-08-07 10:36:47'),(237,30,'Can I get a mortgage if I just switched jobs?','Yes, it is possible to get a mortgage if you just switched jobs.','2025-08-07 10:37:14','2025-08-07 10:37:14'),(238,30,'Is employer category important?','Companies do not need to be listed with banks to secure a mortgage. However, listed companies do make the process easier and faster.','2025-08-07 10:37:46','2025-08-07 10:37:46'),(239,30,'Can I apply if I’m on a limited contract?','Yes, but banks prefer unlimited contracts or may ask for additional documentation or employer assurance.','2025-08-07 10:38:13','2025-08-07 10:38:13'),(240,30,'How does being paid in cash or through foreign accounts affect my application?','Banks usually require verifiable salary through UAE bank accounts — cash income is harder to prove.','2025-08-07 10:38:41','2025-08-07 10:38:41'),(241,30,'What if my business is new — can I still apply?','Most banks require at least 2 years of operating history. However, there are banks who can lend to you based on 6 months of business establishment.','2025-08-07 10:39:08','2025-08-07 10:39:08'),(242,30,'What documents are required for self-employed applicants?','Trade license, 12 months of company bank statements, VAT certificate and report (4 quarters), and audit reports (2 years).','2025-08-07 10:39:35','2025-08-07 10:39:35'),(243,30,'I’m self-employed — am I still eligible?','Yes. You’ll need a valid trade license, audit reports, VAT filing, and company bank statements.','2025-08-07 10:40:04','2025-08-07 10:40:04'),(244,30,'What documents do salaried applicants need?','Emirates ID, passport, Utility bill, salary certificate, 3–6 months of payslips, and bank statements.','2025-08-07 10:40:28','2025-08-07 10:40:28'),(245,30,'Can I apply for a mortgage if I’m salaried?','Yes. Most banks prefer salaried applicants with a steady income and stable employment history.','2025-08-07 10:40:55','2025-08-07 10:40:55'),(246,29,'When do I pay the down payment and closing costs?','On the date of property transfer.','2025-08-07 10:41:40','2025-08-07 10:41:40'),(247,29,'What is the MOU (Memorandum of Understanding)?','It’s a sales agreement between buyer and seller before the official title transfer.','2025-08-07 10:42:07','2025-08-07 10:42:07'),(248,29,'Do I need a real estate agent to apply for a mortgage?','No. The mortgage Preapproval process is independent of property selection. Most clients get a preapproval before they start the property hunt.','2025-08-07 10:42:43','2025-08-07 10:42:43'),(249,29,'Can I use salary transfer to get better mortgage rates?','Yes. Some banks offer lower rates or discounts for salary transfer customers.','2025-08-07 10:43:08','2025-08-07 10:43:08'),(250,29,'Is it mandatory to open an account with the mortgage bank?','Yes, for disbursal and EMI setup. Most banks require this at final approval.','2025-08-07 10:43:34','2025-08-07 10:43:34'),(251,29,'What happens after I get final approval?','You sign the loan offer letter, prepare the down payment, the loan is disbursed and then complete the transfer.','2025-08-07 10:43:59','2025-08-07 10:43:59'),(252,29,'Do I need a sales agreement before applying for a mortgage?','Not for preapproval. But final approval requires a signed sale agreement or MOU.','2025-08-07 10:44:23','2025-08-07 10:44:23'),(253,29,'What’s the difference between a bank and a broker?','A bank offers only its own products. Brokers compare multiple banks and find the best fit for you.','2025-08-07 10:44:57','2025-08-07 10:44:57'),(254,29,'What is the role of a mortgage broker in this process?','At Equifirst Capital Financing we you through the eligibility process, product selection, documentation, and bank coordination.','2025-08-07 10:45:19','2025-08-07 10:45:19'),(255,29,'What happens if my documents are incomplete?','Your application will be delayed or rejected. Always ensure complete and accurate submissions. At Equifirst, we ensure the documentation is complete before its submitted to the bank.','2025-08-07 10:45:51','2025-08-07 10:45:51'),(256,29,'Do documents need to be original or certified?','Banks accept scanned copies for preapproval. Originals may be needed at the final stage.','2025-08-07 10:46:20','2025-08-07 10:46:20'),(257,29,'Who submits documents to the bank?','Either your mortgage broker or you directly — at Equifirst, we handle this for you.','2025-08-07 10:46:44','2025-08-07 10:46:44'),(258,29,'Can I apply for preapproval before selecting a property?','Yes, you can — and should. It’s a smart first step to understand your buying power.','2025-08-07 10:47:41','2025-08-07 10:47:41'),(259,29,'How long does the full mortgage process take?','Usually 4–6 weeks from preapproval to disbursal, depending on speed of documentation and approvals.','2025-08-07 10:48:05','2025-08-07 10:48:05'),(260,29,'What is a property valuation and who does it?','The bank hires a third-party valuer to assess the market value of the property.  The bank will base the loan amount on sale price or valuation – whichever is lower.','2025-08-07 10:48:33','2025-08-07 10:48:33'),(261,29,'What is the difference between preapproval and final approval?','Preapproval checks your eligibility. Final approval is granted once the property is selected and valued, it is the final terms and conditions of the mortgage.','2025-08-07 10:48:58','2025-08-07 10:48:58'),(262,29,'How long does mortgage preapproval take?','Typically 2–10 working days, depending on the bank and document readiness.','2025-08-07 10:49:25','2025-08-07 10:49:25'),(263,29,'Do I need preapproval before I buy a property?','It’s highly recommended. Preapproval gives you a budget and strengthens your negotiation power.','2025-08-07 10:49:46','2025-08-07 10:49:46'),(264,29,'What documents do I need to apply for a mortgage?','Emirates ID, passport, visa, salary certificate or trade license, bank statements, and payslips.','2025-08-07 10:50:11','2025-08-07 10:50:11'),(265,28,'Do I need to pay all fees before the mortgage is approved?','No. Most fees are paid after approval — If there is preapproval fee, that’s the only upfront cost.','2025-08-07 10:51:55','2025-08-07 10:51:55'),(266,28,'How is interest calculated on mortgages?','Interest is usually based on the reducing balance method, charged monthly on the remaining principal.','2025-08-07 10:52:27','2025-08-07 10:52:27'),(267,28,'What is a loan-to-value (LTV) ratio?','It’s the percentage of the property price you borrow. E.g., AED 800K loan on AED 1M property = 80% LTV.','2025-08-07 10:52:56','2025-08-07 10:52:56'),(268,28,'What’s the difference between a reducing rate and a flat rate?','Reducing rate is charged on outstanding balance. Flat rate applies to the full loan — always clarify which applies. Mortgages in the UAE are based on a reducing balance rate.','2025-08-07 10:53:30','2025-08-07 10:53:30'),(269,28,'Are mortgage rates fixed or variable?','Banks offer both. Fixed rates are typically 1–5 years. After that, variable (EIBOR-based) applies.','2025-08-07 10:53:58','2025-08-07 10:53:58'),(270,28,'Are there partial payment penalties?','Most banks allow a certain percentage to be paid as partial prepayments every year.','2025-08-07 10:54:28','2025-08-07 10:54:28'),(271,28,'What are the early settlement charges?','Banks usually charge 1% of the remaining loan amount (or AED 10,000, whichever is lower).','2025-08-07 10:55:00','2025-08-07 10:55:00'),(272,28,'Do I need to pay anything upfront?','Only the valuation fee is typically paid upfront. Other charges are due at property transfer.','2025-08-07 10:55:27','2025-08-07 10:55:27'),(273,28,'What are the fees for using a mortgage broker?','At Equifirst Capital Financing, our consultation is typically free — we’re paid by the bank, not the client.','2025-08-07 10:55:58','2025-08-07 10:55:58'),(274,28,'Is VAT applicable on these fees?','Yes, 5% VAT is applied to most service-based charges like valuations, agency fees, and some bank fees.','2025-08-07 10:56:25','2025-08-07 10:56:25'),(275,28,'Can I negotiate bank fees?','Sometimes — at Equifirst Capital Financing we help you get better deals or fee waivers, especially with strong profiles.','2025-08-07 10:56:51','2025-08-07 10:56:51'),(276,28,'How much does mortgage insurance cost?','Typically 0.015%–0.03% of the loan amount per month. Can vary based on age, loan size, and insurer.','2025-08-07 10:57:29','2025-08-07 10:57:29'),(277,28,'Do I need life or property insurance for a mortgage?','Yes. Banks require both. It’s either bundled with your loan or billed separately.','2025-08-07 10:57:53','2025-08-07 10:57:53'),(278,28,'Are there any hidden fees?','Most costs are disclosed upfront, but watch for early settlement fees, insurance premiums, and broker charges.','2025-08-07 10:58:18','2025-08-07 10:58:18'),(279,28,'Are there valuation fees?','Yes. Property valuation costs range from AED 2,500–3,500, depending on the bank.','2025-08-07 10:58:44','2025-08-07 10:58:44'),(280,28,'What is the bank’s processing fee?','Usually 0.25%–1% + VAT of the loan amount.','2025-08-07 10:59:06','2025-08-07 10:59:06'),(281,28,'Do I have to pay a mortgage registration fee?','Yes. It’s 0.25% of the loan amount + AED 290.','2025-08-07 10:59:35','2025-08-07 11:01:26'),(282,28,'What is the Dubai Land Department (DLD) fee?','4% of the property price + AED 580 admin fee.','2025-08-07 11:00:00','2025-08-07 11:00:00'),(283,28,'What are the closing costs involved in buying a property?','Typically 7% of the property price, including DLD fees, agent fees, mortgage registration, valuation, trustee fees, and bank charges.','2025-08-07 11:00:24','2025-08-07 11:00:24'),(284,28,'How much down payment do I need?','UAE residents: Minimum 20% of the property price.\r\nNon-residents: Typically 35–40%.','2025-08-07 11:00:50','2025-08-07 11:00:50'),(285,27,'Which banks currently have the most competitive fixed or hybrid offers?','This changes monthly. Working with a mortgage broker helps you compare across all banks and find the latest best offers.','2025-08-07 11:02:14','2025-08-07 11:02:14'),(286,27,'Are there green mortgages or sustainability-linked mortgage incentives in the UAE?','A few banks have introduced green mortgages with better rates or terms for environmentally certified buildings, though this is still a niche offering.','2025-08-07 11:02:42','2025-08-07 11:02:42'),(287,27,'Do some mortgage products waive processing fees or offer cashback?','Yes. Promotional offers may include 0% processing fees, partial fee refunds, or cashback on loan disbursal.','2025-08-07 11:03:10','2025-08-07 11:03:10'),(288,27,'Can I apply for a mortgage jointly with a parent, spouse, or sibling?','Yes. Joint mortgages are allowed between immediate family members and can boost eligibility based on combined income.','2025-08-07 11:03:35','2025-08-07 11:03:35'),(289,27,'Is there a special mortgage for buying from developers like Emaar or Damac?','Yes. Many banks have partnerships with developers offering streamlined approvals or better terms for selected projects.','2025-08-07 11:04:06','2025-08-07 11:04:06'),(290,27,'Do banks offer construction loans for building a home on a plot?','Yes, but they require plot ownership, approved plans, and staged disbursement schedules. They are less common and more complex. The maximum borrowing can be 50% of Land value + construction cost.','2025-08-07 11:04:38','2025-08-07 11:04:38'),(291,27,'What mortgage products are available for non-residents?','Non-residents can apply for all mortgage products, except off plan financing with higher down payments (typically 35–40%).','2025-08-07 11:07:20','2025-08-07 11:07:20'),(292,27,'Are there banks that offer pre-approvals valid for more than 60 days?','Yes. Some banks now offer 90 day validity, especially for salaried clients with stable income.','2025-08-07 11:07:47','2025-08-07 11:07:47'),(293,27,'What happens after the fixed-rate period ends?','The mortgage switches to a variable rate (EIBOR + margin) unless you refinance or negotiate another fixed-rate term.','2025-08-07 11:08:19','2025-08-07 11:08:19'),(294,27,'How do staged payment mortgages for under-construction properties work?','The bank disburses money in tranches tied to construction milestones.','2025-08-07 11:08:45','2025-08-07 11:08:45'),(295,27,'Can I take a mortgage for an off-plan property? What’s different in that case?','Yes. Off-plan mortgages have different approval criteria. The bank may release funds in stages based on developer progress and require a larger down payment','2025-08-07 11:09:18','2025-08-07 11:09:18'),(296,27,'Do some banks offer lower rates for government or semi-government employees?','Yes. Employees of government entities often receive preferential rates, lower processing fees, or higher approval chances.','2025-08-07 11:09:42','2025-08-07 11:09:42'),(297,27,'Are there mortgage options tailored for self-employed applicants?','Yes. These typically require audited financials, trade licenses, and bank statements. Loan-to-value ratios may be lower than for salaried applicants.','2025-08-07 11:10:12','2025-08-07 11:10:12'),(298,27,'What’s the difference between Islamic and conventional mortgages in practice?','Islamic banks use structures like Murabaha (cost-plus sale) or Ijara (lease-to-own), while conventional banks charge interest. Practically, the payments are similar.','2025-08-07 11:10:42','2025-08-07 11:10:42'),(299,27,'Can I get a mortgage without transferring my salary to the bank?','Yes, but interest rates are usually slightly higher. Non-salary transfer mortgages are widely available.','2025-08-07 11:11:03','2025-08-07 11:11:03'),(300,27,'Do any banks offer interest-only mortgages?','A few banks offer interest-only options for a limited period (e.g., 1–2 years), mostly for high-net-worth clients.','2025-08-07 11:11:28','2025-08-07 11:11:28'),(301,27,'Are there special mortgage products for first-time buyers in the UAE?','Yes. Some banks offer better loan-to-value (LTV), reduced fees, or promotional fixed-rate products for first-time buyers.','2025-08-07 11:11:53','2025-08-07 11:11:53'),(302,26,'Do I need to be present for final registration?','Yes, or you can assign power of attorney to someone else in some cases.','2025-08-07 11:12:39','2025-08-07 11:12:39'),(303,26,'How do I confirm that my mortgage has been registered?','The mortgage registration is done at the lands department at the time of property transfer. A title deed is issued mentioning that the property is mortgaged to the specific bank.','2025-08-07 11:13:10','2025-08-07 11:13:10'),(304,26,'Can I cancel my application after approval?','Yes, but banks may retain processing fees or valuation charges.','2025-08-07 11:13:37','2025-08-07 11:13:37'),(305,26,'What does \'conditional approval\' mean?','It means the bank is willing to approve subject to certain conditions being met, such as further documents or valuation.','2025-08-07 11:14:01','2025-08-07 11:14:01'),(306,26,'Can I switch banks midway through the application?','Yes, but it can delay the process and you’ll need to restart documentation and valuation.','2025-08-07 11:14:26','2025-08-07 11:14:26'),(307,26,'What should I do if I haven\'t heard back for more than a week?','Contact your mortgage broker or bank contact immediately to avoid unnecessary delays.','2025-08-07 11:14:53','2025-08-07 11:14:53'),(308,26,'How long does it take from pre-approval to disbursal of funds?','Typically 10 – 20 days, depending on the property developer, valuation, and seller liability settlement.','2025-08-07 11:15:39','2025-08-07 11:20:42'),(309,26,'Is it possible to negotiate terms after I get the final offer?','Not usually. Once the final offer is issued there is a cost to change, terms are fixed unless you reapply with a different bank.','2025-08-07 11:20:36','2025-08-07 11:20:36'),(310,26,'Do I get a final offer letter from the bank?','Yes, the bank will issue a binding offer letter with all terms clearly stated.','2025-08-07 11:21:34','2025-08-07 11:21:34'),(311,26,'What happens if my mortgage is rejected?','Your broker can try with another bank, or help address the reason for rejection (e.g., liabilities, credit score).','2025-08-07 11:21:59','2025-08-07 11:21:59'),(312,26,'Can I speed up the mortgage approval process?','Submitting complete, accurate documents and being responsive to follow-ups helps avoid delays. At Equifirst, we make sure all documents are complete and have constant follow-ups with the banks in order to ensure speedy approvals.','2025-08-07 11:27:57','2025-08-07 11:27:57'),(313,26,'What can delay my mortgage application?','Incomplete documents, property legal issues, valuation delays, or missed communications from the client.','2025-08-07 11:29:20','2025-08-07 11:29:20'),(314,26,'How will I know if the bank has done the property valuation?','In order to initiate the valuation, a valuation fee needs to be paid to the bank. The valuation company will contact your agent to schedule the valuation. Once the valuation is complete – the report is shared with you.','2025-08-07 11:29:57','2025-08-07 11:29:57'),(315,26,'How long is the pre-approval valid for?','Generally 30–90 days, depending on the bank.','2025-08-07 11:30:30','2025-08-07 11:30:30'),(316,26,'What are the different stages in a mortgage application?','Typically: Pre-approval → Property valuation → Final approval → Mortgage registration and Transfer.','2025-08-07 11:31:03','2025-08-07 11:31:03'),(317,26,'Can I track the status of my mortgage application online?','Some banks offer online portals, but most tracking is still done manually via your broker.','2025-08-07 11:31:35','2025-08-07 11:31:35'),(318,26,'Will I be informed if additional documents are needed by the bank?','Yes, your broker will contact you if anything is missing or needs clarification.','2025-08-07 11:32:10','2025-08-07 11:32:10'),(319,26,'How long does it take to get pre-approval after submission?','On average, 2–10 working days for salaried clients, and 5–10 working days for self-employed applicants.','2025-08-07 11:32:36','2025-08-07 11:32:36'),(320,26,'How do I know if my mortgage application has been submitted to the bank?','You’ll usually receive a confirmation from your mortgage advisor or broker, and some banks send a submission reference number.','2025-08-07 11:33:01','2025-08-07 11:33:01'),(321,25,'What if I lose my job or can’t pay anymore?','You must notify your bank immediately. They may offer restructuring, but legal consequences apply if ignored.','2025-08-07 11:34:46','2025-08-07 11:34:46'),(322,25,'Can I change my repayment currency?','No — UAE mortgages must be repaid in AED, even if you earn in a foreign currency.','2025-08-07 11:35:19','2025-08-07 11:35:19'),(323,25,'Does my credit score improve as I repay the mortgage?','Yes, consistent repayment positively impacts your credit history and score.','2025-08-07 11:35:48','2025-08-07 11:35:48'),(324,25,'Can I access a mortgage statement or repayment schedule?','Yes, either via online banking or by requesting it from the bank.','2025-08-07 11:36:20','2025-08-07 11:36:20'),(325,25,'Will I get a NOC after I settle the loan?','Yes, the bank provides a Clearance Certificate once the mortgage is cleared, required to remove the lien.','2025-08-07 11:36:55','2025-08-07 11:36:55'),(326,25,'How is my outstanding loan balance calculated?','It’s based on the principal remaining, not including interest due for future months.','2025-08-07 11:37:28','2025-08-07 11:37:28'),(327,25,'Can I refinance if my property value has dropped?','It’s more difficult. Banks typically revalue the property and limit the loan amount accordingly.','2025-08-07 11:37:58','2025-08-07 11:37:58'),(328,25,'Can I switch from a variable rate to a fixed rate mortgage later?','Yes, some banks allow it — usually at a fee or during specific review windows.','2025-08-07 11:38:21','2025-08-07 11:38:21'),(329,25,'Can I transfer my mortgage to another property?','Not directly. You’ll likely need to close the current mortgage and apply for a new one for the other property.','2025-08-07 11:38:46','2025-08-07 11:38:46'),(330,25,'Can I get a payment holiday?','Some banks offer short-term relief, but it usually needs to be requested in advance with justification.','2025-08-07 11:39:22','2025-08-07 11:39:22'),(331,25,'What happens if I miss a mortgage payment?','The bank may charge a late payment fee and report the default to the credit bureau (Al Etihad Credit Bureau).','2025-08-07 11:39:47','2025-08-07 11:39:47'),(332,25,'How long does it take to refinance a mortgage?','Usually 2–3 weeks, depending on the bank’s process and valuation timing.','2025-08-07 11:40:25','2025-08-07 11:40:25'),(333,25,'What documents do I need to refinance?','Similar to a new application — ID, income proof, property details, current mortgage balance.','2025-08-07 11:40:51','2025-08-07 11:40:51'),(334,25,'Is refinancing worth it?','If the new rate is significantly lower or your financial situation has improved, yes. Always factor in switching fees.','2025-08-07 11:41:22','2025-08-07 11:41:22'),(335,25,'Can I refinance my mortgage with another bank?','Yes, this is common. You can refinance to get better rates or change loan terms.','2025-08-07 11:41:51','2025-08-07 11:41:51'),(336,25,'How much is the early settlement fee if I want to close the mortgage early?','It’s typically 1% of the outstanding loan amount or AED 10,000 — whichever is lower.','2025-08-07 11:42:18','2025-08-07 11:42:18'),(337,25,'Can I make extra payments toward my mortgage?','Yes, some banks offer free partial settlements. Else the partial settlement fees may apply (commonly 1% or AED 10,000 (whichever is lower) of the extra amount paid).','2025-08-07 11:42:50','2025-08-07 11:42:50'),(338,25,'Can I change my repayment date?','Some banks allow it once during your loan term, but it depends on the institution’s policy.','2025-08-07 11:43:12','2025-08-07 11:43:12'),(339,25,'How are mortgage repayments collected in the UAE?','Most banks collect monthly payments via direct debit from your UAE bank account.','2025-08-07 11:43:34','2025-08-07 11:43:34'),(340,25,'When do I start repaying my mortgage?','Usually one month after disbursal. Your offer letter will specify the exact date.','2025-08-07 11:43:56','2025-08-07 11:43:56'),(341,24,'Can I track EIBOR myself?','Yes. It’s published daily by the UAE Central Bank at: www.centralbank.ae','2025-08-07 12:47:38','2025-08-07 12:47:38'),(342,24,'What is a teaser rate?','A temporarily low interest rate offered at the beginning, which then increases after a set period.','2025-08-07 12:48:06','2025-08-07 12:48:06'),(343,24,'What factors affect the rate offered to me?','Income, employment type, credit score, loan amount, down payment, and bank relationship.','2025-08-07 12:48:34','2025-08-07 12:48:34'),(344,24,'Is there a cap on how high my variable rate can go?','Some banks apply a cap, others don’t. Always check the terms in your offer letter.','2025-08-07 12:49:02','2025-08-07 12:49:02'),(345,24,'How do I decide between fixed and variable?','Consider your risk tolerance, expected length of stay, market outlook, and whether rates are likely to rise or fall.','2025-08-07 12:49:38','2025-08-07 12:49:38'),(346,24,'Can I refinance to get a better interest rate?','Yes, many clients refinance when rates drop or their credit profile improves.','2025-08-07 12:50:08','2025-08-07 12:50:08'),(347,24,'Can the bank increase my fixed rate mid-term?','No — fixed rates are contractually protected for the duration agreed.','2025-08-07 12:51:11','2025-08-07 12:51:11'),(348,24,'Do Islamic home finance products have interest rates?','Technically no — they charge profit rates, but they function similarly to conventional rates.','2025-08-07 12:51:36','2025-08-07 12:51:36'),(349,24,'Can my interest rate go below the original fixed rate?','Yes, if you\'re on a variable rate and the EIBOR drops significantly.','2025-08-07 12:52:14','2025-08-07 12:52:14'),(350,24,'What happens if interest rates rise?','If you\'re on a variable rate, your EMI (monthly installment) will increase.  If you are on a fixed rate – the rate remains unchanged.','2025-08-07 12:52:46','2025-08-07 12:52:46'),(351,24,'Can I lock in a fixed rate for the entire loan term?','No — most banks offer fixed terms for 1–5 years, after which it reverts to a variable rate.','2025-08-07 12:53:12','2025-08-07 12:53:12'),(352,24,'Are there any 0% interest mortgages?','No, currently there are no 0% interest mortgages available in the UAE.','2025-08-07 12:53:38','2025-08-07 12:53:38'),(353,24,'Do non-residents pay higher rates?','Usually yes, due to perceived risk and limited bank options.','2025-08-07 12:54:05','2025-08-07 12:54:05'),(354,24,'What is the average mortgage rate in the UAE?','As of 2025:\r\nSalary Resident:  3.95%–4. 5%\r\nSelf employed Resident:   4.2% - 5%\r\nNon Resident:   4.8% - 6%','2025-08-07 12:54:42','2025-08-07 12:54:54'),(355,24,'Can I negotiate the rate with the bank?','Yes, especially if you have a strong profile or competing offers.','2025-08-07 12:55:22','2025-08-07 12:55:22'),(356,24,'When is a variable rate better?','If you expect interest rates to fall or want flexibility (e.g., planning to sell the property soon).','2025-08-07 12:55:52','2025-08-07 13:00:29'),(357,24,'Is it safer to choose a fixed-rate mortgage?','Yes, for stability. Fixed rates are ideal when you want predictable payments and expect rates to rise.','2025-08-07 12:56:27','2025-08-07 12:56:27'),(358,24,'Do fixed-rate mortgages have higher interest than variable?','Usually yes — banks charge a premium for locking in your rate and giving you stability.','2025-08-07 12:56:55','2025-08-07 12:56:55'),(359,24,'Can I switch from variable to fixed later?','Banks allow the switch, but the terms will be based on the current market conditions.','2025-08-07 12:57:24','2025-08-07 12:57:24'),(360,24,'What is a reversion rate?','This is the rate your mortgage moves to after your fixed rate period ends. Often higher than your initial rate.','2025-08-07 12:57:57','2025-08-07 12:57:57'),(361,24,'How is a variable mortgage rate calculated?','Usually: EIBOR + bank margin. For example, EIBOR at 4% + 1.99% margin = 5.99% interest.','2025-08-07 12:58:26','2025-08-07 12:58:26'),(362,24,'What is EIBOR?','EIBOR is the rate at which UAE banks lend to each other. It forms the base for most variable mortgage rates.','2025-08-07 12:58:56','2025-08-07 12:58:56'),(363,24,'How often do variable rates change?','Typically monthly or quarterly, based on the EIBOR (Emirates Interbank Offered Rate) or another benchmark.','2025-08-07 12:59:24','2025-08-07 12:59:24'),(364,24,'Which is better — fixed or variable rate?','Fixed rates offer stability; variable rates can be cheaper if market rates drop. The right choice depends on your risk appetite.','2025-08-07 12:59:47','2025-08-07 12:59:47'),(365,24,'What’s the difference between a fixed and variable mortgage rate?','A fixed rate stays the same for a set period (e.g., 3–5 years). A variable rate changes based on market rates.','2025-08-07 13:00:18','2025-08-07 13:00:18'),(366,23,'Can my loan be rejected due to my nationality?','Not directly, but some banks have restrictions on certain passports or non-resident categories.','2025-08-08 09:27:55','2025-08-08 09:27:55'),(367,23,'Which banks offer pre-construction (off-plan) mortgages?','Only a few — and they usually have stricter criteria, including approved developers.','2025-08-08 09:28:31','2025-08-08 09:28:31'),(368,23,'Is there a bank that waives processing fees?','Some banks run limited-time offers or promotions where fees are reduced or waived.','2025-08-08 09:29:05','2025-08-08 09:29:05'),(369,23,'Do all banks charge early settlement fees?','Most do — 1% of the outstanding amount, capped at AED 10,000.','2025-08-08 09:29:40','2025-08-08 09:29:40'),(370,23,'Do all banks require a life insurance policy?','Most do. It’s bundled with the loan and can either be upfront or annual.','2025-08-08 09:30:14','2025-08-08 09:30:14'),(371,23,'Can I apply to multiple banks at the same time?','Yes, especially through a broker — but keep in mind that too many credit checks can affect your score.','2025-08-08 09:30:43','2025-08-08 09:30:43'),(372,23,'Why do rates differ so much between banks?','It depends on each bank’s risk appetite, funding cost, and promotional offers.','2025-08-08 09:31:10','2025-08-08 09:31:10'),(373,23,'Do some banks have faster processing times?','Yes — some are known to process applications in under 2 days, others may take longer.','2025-08-08 09:31:35','2025-08-08 09:31:35'),(374,23,'Can banks reject my application even after pre-approval?','Yes — if documentation doesn\'t match or creditworthiness changes before final approval.','2025-08-08 09:32:45','2025-08-08 09:32:45'),(375,23,'Are all mortgage tenures the same across banks?','Not always. Most offer up to 25 years, but some may have shorter maximum tenures depending on age and loan size.','2025-08-08 09:33:12','2025-08-08 09:33:12'),(376,23,'What’s the minimum salary accepted by banks?','Generally AED 10,000 per month, but some banks may go lower for government employees.','2025-08-08 09:34:10','2025-08-08 09:34:10'),(377,23,'Do banks allow co-applicants?','Yes — most allow a spouse or close family member as a co-applicant to increase loan eligibility.','2025-08-08 09:34:41','2025-08-08 09:34:41'),(378,23,'Do all banks accept the same types of income?','No — some banks accept rental income, others only salary. Some require audited financials for business owners.','2025-08-08 09:35:12','2025-08-08 09:35:12'),(379,23,'Do all banks require a property valuation?','Yes, and each bank uses its own approved valuation firms. Charges may vary.','2025-08-08 09:35:37','2025-08-08 09:35:37'),(380,23,'Why do some banks ask for more documents than others?','It depends on the bank’s internal risk assessment, compliance, and policy.','2025-08-08 09:36:08','2025-08-08 09:36:08'),(381,23,'Can I choose the bank I apply with?','Yes — your broker can guide you, but the final decision is yours.','2025-08-08 09:36:36','2025-08-08 09:36:36'),(382,23,'Do Islamic banks offer different types of mortgages?','Yes, they offer Shariah-compliant products like Murabaha or Ijara instead of conventional interest-based loans.','2025-08-08 09:37:02','2025-08-08 09:37:02'),(383,23,'Which banks offer mortgages to non-residents?','A few UAE banks do — options and terms are more limited than for residents.','2025-08-08 09:37:31','2025-08-08 09:37:31'),(384,23,'Which banks are best for first-time buyers?','It varies based on your profile. Some banks are more flexible with income or offer better rates for salaried clients.','2025-08-08 09:37:58','2025-08-08 09:37:58'),(385,23,'Do all banks offer the same mortgage products?','No — each bank has different eligibility criteria, rates, tenures, and product structures.','2025-08-08 09:38:21','2025-08-08 09:38:21'),(386,22,'Will a high score guarantee approval?','No — but it increases your chances. Banks still assess your overall financial profile.','2025-08-08 09:42:54','2025-08-08 09:42:54'),(387,22,'Do supplementary cards affect my credit score?','No — only the primary cardholder’s usage and payments are reported.','2025-08-08 09:43:25','2025-08-08 09:43:25'),(388,22,'Does a loan rejection hurt my score?','Not directly. But the inquiry that led to the rejection may slightly reduce your score.','2025-08-08 09:43:53','2025-08-08 09:43:53'),(389,22,'Can I dispute my AECB credit report?','Yes — if you find an error, you can raise a complaint with AECB to investigate.','2025-08-08 11:51:51','2025-08-08 11:51:51'),(390,22,'Do bounced rent cheques affect my score?','Yes — bounced cheques of any kind negatively affect your credit report.','2025-08-08 11:52:20','2025-08-08 11:52:20'),(391,22,'What is a credit report vs. a credit score?','The report shows your full credit history. The score is a number summarizing your risk level.','2025-08-08 11:53:12','2025-08-08 11:53:12'),(392,22,'Is credit score the only thing banks look at?','No — they also consider income, employment, liabilities, and property details.','2025-08-08 11:53:39','2025-08-08 11:53:39'),(393,22,'Will applying for multiple mortgages affect my score?','Yes — multiple hard inquiries from banks can temporarily lower your score.','2025-08-08 11:54:08','2025-08-08 11:54:08'),(394,22,'Can I get a mortgage without a credit history?','It\'s difficult. Some banks may require alternative documentation or collateral.','2025-08-08 11:54:33','2025-08-08 11:54:33'),(395,22,'How long does negative data stay on my report?','Typically 24 months — serious issues like loan defaults may stay longer.','2025-08-08 11:55:02','2025-08-08 11:55:02'),(396,22,'Does having multiple credit cards reduce my score?','Not necessarily. It depends on how you manage your balances and repayments.','2025-08-08 11:55:36','2025-08-08 11:55:36'),(397,22,'What affects my AECB credit score?','Loan repayments, credit card usage, bounced cheques, late payments, and number of inquiries.','2025-08-08 11:56:08','2025-08-08 11:56:08'),(398,22,'How can I improve my credit score?','Pay bills and loans on time, reduce credit card usage, and avoid late payments or bounced cheques.','2025-08-08 11:57:19','2025-08-08 11:57:19'),(399,22,'Can I apply for a mortgage with a low credit score?','It depends on the bank. Some may reject, others may approve with higher rates or more documents.','2025-08-08 11:57:41','2025-08-08 11:57:41'),(400,22,'What is considered a bad credit score?','Anything below 500 may cause your mortgage to be declined or heavily restricted.','2025-08-08 11:58:06','2025-08-08 11:58:06'),(401,22,'Does checking my own credit score affect it?','No — checking your score through AECB is a soft inquiry and has no impact.','2025-08-08 11:58:30','2025-08-08 11:58:30'),(402,22,'How do I check my AECB credit score?','You can check it through the AECB app or website by verifying your Emirates ID and paying a small fee.','2025-08-08 11:59:11','2025-08-08 11:59:11'),(403,22,'What is a good credit score in the UAE?','A score above 700 is considered good. Scores range from 300 (poor) to 900 (excellent).','2025-08-08 11:59:36','2025-08-08 11:59:36'),(404,22,'Why is my credit score important for a mortgage?','Banks use your score to assess how risky it is to lend to you. A higher score improves your chances of approval and better rates.','2025-08-08 12:00:01','2025-08-08 12:00:01'),(405,22,'What is the Al Etihad Credit Bureau (AECB)?','AECB is the UAE’s official credit bureau. It collects and maintains credit information for individuals and businesses.','2025-08-08 12:00:28','2025-08-08 12:00:28'),(406,21,'Is there any VAT or fee included in the down payment?','No — VAT and other fees (DLD, broker fee, etc.) are separate and not counted as down payment.','2025-08-08 12:01:19','2025-08-08 12:01:19'),(407,21,'Can I use my gratuity or end-of-service benefits?','Yes — but documentation showing the amount and timing will be required.','2025-08-08 12:01:42','2025-08-08 12:14:56'),(408,21,'What if I don’t have enough for the down payment?','You may need to delay the purchase, find a co-applicant, or look at lower-priced properties.','2025-08-08 12:02:07','2025-08-08 12:15:05'),(409,21,'Does a higher down payment improve my chances?','Yes — it reduces the bank’s risk and may lead to better interest rates or faster approval.','2025-08-08 12:02:50','2025-08-08 12:15:11'),(410,21,'Can I increase the loan amount after approval?','Only if the bank re-assesses your profile and the property supports the increase.','2025-08-08 12:03:12','2025-08-08 12:15:18'),(411,21,'Can I reduce my LTV after pre-approval?','Yes — if you increase your down payment. This may also improve your loan terms.','2025-08-08 12:03:34','2025-08-08 12:15:24'),(412,21,'Does the LTV change based on property type?','Yes — off-plan properties, commercial real estate, and high-value properties often require higher down payments.','2025-08-08 12:03:57','2025-08-08 12:15:28'),(413,21,'What happens if the valuation is lower than the price?','You’ll need to cover the difference in cash, in addition to the down payment.','2025-08-08 12:04:23','2025-08-08 12:15:34'),(414,21,'Is the down payment calculated on property price or valuation?','The down payment is always calculated based on property price. However, if your valuation comes lower, then you will have to furnish the difference.','2025-08-08 12:05:00','2025-08-08 12:05:00'),(415,21,'Can I use money from outside the UAE for the down payment?','Yes — but you’ll need to show the source and transfer proof for compliance.','2025-08-08 12:05:27','2025-08-08 12:05:27'),(416,21,'Do banks accept company-provided down payments?','Only in certain cases, with proper documentation and approval — usually for company-owned properties.','2025-08-08 12:05:52','2025-08-08 12:05:52'),(417,21,'Can family members give me the down payment?','Yes — banks may accept gifted funds with a gift letter and supporting documentation.','2025-08-08 12:06:17','2025-08-08 12:06:17'),(418,21,'Can I use a credit card for down payment?','No — credit card advances or loans cannot be used as down payments.','2025-08-08 12:08:48','2025-08-08 12:08:48'),(419,21,'Do banks verify the source of my down payment?','Yes — especially if the down payment is large or coming from overseas. Proof of funds is usually required.','2025-08-08 12:09:14','2025-08-08 12:13:49'),(420,21,'Can my down payment be paid in installments?','No — it must be available in full at the time of purchase.','2025-08-08 12:09:53','2025-08-08 12:10:00'),(421,21,'Are there any exceptions to the down payment rule?','No, the down payment requirement is a UAE Central Bank guideline.','2025-08-08 12:10:23','2025-08-08 12:13:56'),(422,21,'Can I borrow the down payment from another bank?','No — banks require the down payment to come from your own sources (savings or gifted funds).','2025-08-08 12:10:48','2025-08-08 12:10:48'),(423,21,'How much down payment is required in the UAE?','20% for residents, for properties <5million AED.   30% for residents, for properties > 5million AED.\r\n35% for non-residents.\r\n50% for off plan properties.\r\n40% for commercial properties.','2025-08-08 12:11:17','2025-08-08 12:11:17'),(424,21,'What is Loan-to-Value (LTV)?','LTV is the percentage of the property value that the bank is willing to finance. For example, 80% LTV means you pay 20% downpayment.','2025-08-08 12:12:57','2025-08-08 12:12:57'),(425,21,'What is a down payment?','A down payment is a client\'s contribution towards the property. The bank finances the rest via a mortgage.','2025-08-08 12:13:22','2025-08-08 12:13:22');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `faqs` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

